# Pine sources carry deployment hashes: their exact bytes are compared against
# the script saved on TradingView and against hashes recorded in closure
# evidence, so a checkout must never decide their line endings. core.autocrlf
# would otherwise hand out different bytes per machine and every recorded
# sha256 would stop matching, silently and without a visible character change.
*.pine text eol=lf

# These two are pinned to CRLF because that is what their RECORDED P2 closure
# hashes were computed over (3d6d10df... and 17e6d56b..., asserted in
# tests/unit/test_p2_*.py and BTRC_V1_P2_STRUCTURE_CLOSURE.md). Git stores them
# as LF, so today those hashes only match on a machine with autocrlf=true --
# pinning makes the closure evidence reproducible instead of accidental.
# Do not "tidy" these to LF without re-deriving the P2 closure hashes.
tradingview/btmm_poi_btrc_scanner_v1.pine text eol=crlf
tradingview/btmm_poi_btrc_scanner_p2_parity_probe.pine text eol=crlf
